note for test at the latch on both sides of the CMP immediate limit: K = 4095 fits the 12-bit field
note (CMP Xi, #K), K = 4096 does not (matconst then CMP Xi, Xk); 4095 + 4096 passes (exit 0). A latch that
note encodes 4096 as an immediate (bit 22: CMP Xi, #0, LSL #12) leaves after 1 pass; 4095 + 1 - 8191 wraps
note and the int conversion traps 5 (exit 105)
om2
fn main to int
a = ulong 0
for i ulong 4095
a = add a 1
end
b = ulong 0
for j ulong 4096
b = add b 1
end
ret int sub add a b 8191
end
